<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefan Stambolov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1854–1895</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefan Stambolov was a Bulgarian revolutionary and statesman. As regent after the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-of-battenberg">Alexander of Battenberg</a> in 1886, he secured the election of Ferdinand of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a>, and as prime minister from 1887 to 1894 he ruled firmly, resisting Russian influence and building up the state. He was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofia">Sofia</a> in 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-stambolov.jpg" alt="Stefan Stambolov" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georgi Danchov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stefan_Stambolov_by_Georgi_Danchov_Zografina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
